@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@cindex introduction
@cindex overview
@cindex ERT

The List Manager Test Suite provides comprehensive test coverage for the
@code{list-manager.el} package using Emacs Lisp Regression Testing (ERT).

@section Purpose

The test suite serves multiple purposes:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Verify that all functions work correctly.

@item
Prevent regressions when making changes.

@item
Document expected behavior through examples.

@item
Provide confidence for MELPA submission.
@end itemize

@section Test Coverage

The test suite contains 130 tests covering:

@itemize @bullet
@item
List conversion functions (numbered, dash, asterisk, plus lists).

@item
Checklist operations (extract, cut, convert).

@item
LaTeX environment creation.

@item
750words formatting recovery.

@item
Text manipulation utilities.

@item
Edge cases and boundary conditions.

@item
Multi-function integration workflows.
@end itemize

@node Running Tests
@chapter Running Tests

@cindex running tests
@cindex ERT commands

This chapter explains how to run the List Manager test suite.

@section Running All Tests

To run all tests interactively:

@example
M-x ert RET t RET
@end example

@section Running Tests by Pattern

To run tests matching a specific pattern:

@example
M-x ert RET "list-manager" RET
@end example

This runs all tests whose names contain ``list-manager''.

@section Running a Specific Test

To run a single test:

@example
M-x ert RET list-manager-test-numbered-list-to-latex-items-basic RET
@end example

@section Running Tests in Batch Mode

For continuous integration or command-line testing:

@example
emacs --batch -Q -L . \
  -l list-manager.el \
  -l list-manager-test.el \
  -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit
@end example

@section Running Tests with Make

If using the provided Makefile:

@example
cd /path/to/list-manager
make test
@end example

@section Interpreting Results

ERT displays results in a special buffer:

@table @samp
@item passed
The test succeeded.

@item FAILED
The test failed.  Click on the test name for details.

@item skipped
The test was skipped (usually due to missing dependencies).
@end table

Expected output for a successful run:

@example
Ran 130 tests, 130 results as expected, 0 unexpected
@end example

@node Test Categories
@chapter Test Categories

@cindex test categories
@cindex test organization

The tests are organized into several categories.

@section Unit Tests

Unit tests verify individual functions in isolation.  Each test:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Tests a single function.

@item
Uses minimal setup.

@item
Verifies specific input/output behavior.
@end itemize

Example categories:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{list-manager-test-numbered-list-*} --- Numbered list conversions.

@item
@code{list-manager-test-dash-list-*} --- Dash list conversions.

@item
@code{list-manager-test-extract-unchecked-*} --- Unchecked item extraction.

@item
@code{list-manager-test-convert-*} --- List format conversions.
@end itemize

@section Integration Tests

Integration tests verify that multiple functions work together correctly.
They test common workflows:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{list-manager-integration-test-org-to-latex-workflow}

@item
@code{list-manager-integration-test-latex-formatting-recovery}

@item
@code{list-manager-integration-test-extract-and-cut-workflow}
@end itemize

@section Edge Case Tests

Edge case tests verify behavior at boundaries:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Empty buffers and regions.

@item
Single-item lists.

@item
Special characters (unicode, LaTeX symbols).

@item
Very long items.

@item
Nested brackets.
@end itemize

@section Performance Tests

Performance tests ensure operations complete in reasonable time:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{list-manager-performance-test-large-list} --- Tests handling of
1000-item lists.
@end itemize

Performance tests are tagged with @code{:slow} and can be excluded
from regular test runs.

@section Regression Tests

Regression tests pin the behavior of bugs fixed in the 1.0.0 release so
they cannot return:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{list-manager-test-enhanced-plain-item} and
@code{list-manager-test-enhanced-all-items-converted} --- the enhanced
conversion inserts backslashes literally and converts every item.

@item
@code{list-manager-test-repair-stripped-item-list-idempotent} and
@code{list-manager-test-repair-stripped-item-list-preserves-itemize} ---
the repair command is idempotent and never splits words such as
@code{itemize}.

@item
@code{list-manager-test-org-or-latex-add-periods-org} and
@code{list-manager-test-beginning-of-list-at-bob} --- the first item of
a list at the start of the buffer is handled correctly.

@item
@code{list-manager-test-restore-latex-formatting} --- the combined
750words recovery command runs without error.
@end itemize

